  entryReasons:
    earlyDaysReasons:
    - Home after afternoon classes.
    - Back from a school parent meeting.
    - Collecting textbooks from the depot.
    midDaysReasons:
    - From the closed school. Managing materials.
    - Curriculum materials from the regional office.
    - Bringing home papers to grade.
    finalDaysReasons:
    - Back from teaching at the Lenin street shelter.
    - Home to my daughters. They're waiting.
    - Returning home. School is suspended.
  invalidEntryReasons:
    earlyDaysReasons:
    - Back from my son's football practice.
    - First week teaching. I hope they like me.
    - Skipped class. Children can teach themselves.
    midDaysReasons:
    - Collecting my grandchildren from their mother's.
    - School materials aren't my concern anymore.
    - Going home to my ground-floor flat.
    finalDaysReasons:
    - Daughters moved out years ago. Going home alone.
    - Visiting the shelter. I stopped teaching long ago.
    - Collecting my school retirement papers.
  entryDialogues:
    lastVerdict: 0
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - My papers. Always in order. Unlike some of my students.
    - I trust you have a checklist. Checklists make this faster.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - You are slower than yesterday's officer. It is fine. Everyone has a pace.
    - Poor light in here. Not a complaint. A note.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - My daughters are waiting on the fourth floor. Let us be efficient.
    - Longer line, smaller staff, every day. Someone should address that.
